# Rig/agentic engineering anchor

Apply when the task touches Rig, LLM/model calls, agents, tools, hooks, agent memory, retrieval/RAG, MCP, structured model output, or multi-agent orchestration.

## Hard invariants

- An LLM is a component inside deterministic application architecture.
- Use the least autonomy required; deterministic workflows own deterministic policy.
- Every autonomous run is bounded by host-controlled limits.
- Tools are privileged capability boundaries and receive least privilege.
- Trusted user/tenant/authorization context is host-controlled, not model-selected.
- High-impact side effects require deterministic policy and approval where appropriate.
- Structured output still requires domain validation.
- Retrieved/external content is untrusted instruction data.
- Material agent behavior requires deterministic harness tests and representative evals.

